    "ex-linear-elasticity-p1-volumetric-locking-fixed-mesh": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice. On $D=(0,1)^2$, let $c=(1/2,1/2)$ and split the square into the four triangles joining $c$ to consecutive corners. The continuous P1 vector space with zero boundary values has no nonzero elementwise divergence-free field. Choose a nonzero smooth compactly supported divergence-free displacement $u$ and set $f=-\\operatorname{div}(2\\varepsilon(u))$. Then $u$ solves the continuous model with $\\mu=1$ for every finite $\\lambda\\ge0$, but the P1 displacement Galerkin solutions on this fixed mesh tend to zero as $\\lambda\\to\\infty$, so their $V$-norm error tends to $\\|u\\|_V>0$. The mini mixed pair on the same mesh retains the $\\lambda$-uniform best-approximation estimate of [[thm-nearly-incompressible-elasticity-mini-uniform-stability-and-error]]. This is a fixed-mesh obstruction, not a mesh-uniform P1 rate."
